B.aCI=new A.eh("The short version","\u2022 ShieldPal has no account, no login and no servers of its own. We do not collect, store or sell your personal data.\n\u2022 Messages, notifications, your list of apps, contacts and Deep Scan results are analysed ON YOUR PHONE and stay there.\n\u2022 A few optional features send a small piece of data to a third-party service, only when you use them. They are all listed in section 3.\n\u2022 No ads. No tracking or analytics. We never sell or share your data.")
B.aCO=new A.eh("1. What stays on your phone","\u2022 Live Guard reads the text of new notifications (WhatsApp, SMS, Telegram\u2026) to look for scam links and messages. The check happens on the device. If something dangerous is found, a short snippet plus the app and chat name are saved in your Threat Log on the phone. Nothing is uploaded.\n\u2022 Message Check, the scam-detecting AI model, Number Check, Safe QR (camera pictures never leave the phone), Password strength, Family Safe-Word, the pet, coins and settings all work on the device.\n\u2022 2FA Vault secrets, API keys you add and your app-lock PIN are stored encrypted (Android Keystore). The PIN is stored only as a hash.\n\u2022 Deep Scan reads your installed apps, their permissions and your phone's security settings on the device. The result is never uploaded.\n\u2022 Contacts (optional): if you allow it, ShieldPal looks up the name you saved for a number you are checking. This happens on the phone; contacts are never uploaded or stored by ShieldPal.")
B.aCG=new A.eh("2. Account and identity","ShieldPal needs no sign-up. We do not know who you are, and we do not collect your name, e-mail, phone number, location or advertising ID.")
B.aCH=new A.eh("3. What can leave your phone (optional)","Only when you use the feature. Everything is sent over HTTPS.\n\n\u2022 Link Check \xb7 Cloudflare Security DNS: the domain name of the link (for example \"example.com\"), never the full address or any personal detail. You can switch this off in Settings \u2192 Online services & AI.\n\u2022 Link Check \xb7 Google Safe Browsing (only if you add your own key): the link address.\n\u2022 Link Check \xb7 urlscan.io cloud browser (only if you add your own key and switch it on): the link address. urlscan.io opens the page far away from your phone and keeps the scan unlisted.\n\u2022 Password Check \xb7 Have I Been Pwned: only the first 5 characters of the password's SHA-1 fingerprint (k-anonymity). Never the password itself.\n\u2022 Pal AI \xb7 Free online AI (pollinations.ai): the text of your chat with Pal AI, only after you agree to it. Do not type passwords or codes into the chat. Turn it off any time in Settings; Pal AI also works fully offline.\n\u2022 Pal AI \xb7 Claude by Anthropic (only if you add your own key): your chat messages, sent with your own key. Anthropic's privacy policy applies.\n\u2022 Shield VPN: this is a local VPN on your phone. It does not send your traffic to ShieldPal or to any VPN server. Only your device's DNS lookups (the domain names your apps ask for) go to the DNS provider you choose in the app (Cloudflare, Google, Quad9, AdGuard or OpenDNS) \u2014 the same kind of lookups your phone normally sends to your mobile network. It does not hide your IP address.\n\u2022 Remote VPN (optional): runs a WireGuard config that YOU paste. All your traffic then goes to the VPN server named in that config, so that provider can see it. ShieldPal stores the config encrypted on your phone only and never sends it anywhere else.\n\u2022 Check my IP (optional button): asks ipwho.is for your public IP and country.\n\u2022 Spoken warnings use the Android text-to-speech engine on your phone.\n\nThese services have their own privacy policies. ShieldPal gets none of this data.")
B.aCz=new A.eh("4. Permissions and why we ask",'\u2022 Internet \u2014 the optional online checks above.\n\u2022 Notifications \u2014 to show threat alerts.\n\u2022 Notification access \u2014 Live Guard (reading notifications on the device to find scams). You turn it on yourself in Android settings and can turn it off any time.\n\u2022 Installed apps list (QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES) \u2014 Deep Scan and new-app warnings. The list stays on the device.\n\u2022 Request delete packages \u2014 the one-tap "Remove" button for dangerous apps (you still confirm).\n\u2022 Screen-lock strength \u2014 to tell you if your lock is weak (never your PIN).\n\u2022 Camera \u2014 Safe QR scanner. Pictures are not saved or uploaded.\n\u2022 Biometrics \u2014 fingerprint / face unlock for the app lock.\n\u2022 Contacts (optional) \u2014 to show the saved name of a number.\n\u2022 VPN service \u2014 the local DNS filter (Shield VPN). You approve the Android VPN dialog yourself.')
B.aCK=new A.eh("5. Security","Online requests use HTTPS. Secrets are encrypted with the Android Keystore. The PIN is hashed. The app lock can use your fingerprint or face. ShieldPal does not back up its data to the cloud (allowBackup is off).")
B.aCD=new A.eh("6. Children and teens","ShieldPal is made for everyone, including teenagers and families. It does not create accounts and does not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, including children under 13.")
B.aCM=new A.eh("7. Your choices and deleting your data",'\u2022 Settings \u2192 Privacy \u2192 "Delete all my data" erases everything ShieldPal stores on your phone: settings, threat log, 2FA codes, keys, PIN and pet progress.\n\u2022 Uninstalling the app also removes all of it.\n\u2022 You can revoke any permission or turn off Live Guard and Shield VPN in Android settings at any time.\n\u2022 We hold no data about you on any server, so there is nothing to request from us. For data held by a third-party service, contact that service.')
B.aCF=new A.eh("8. Changes to this policy","If features change, we update this policy here and in the app, and change the date above.")
B.aCB=new A.eh("9. Contact",u.x)
B.afN=s([B.aCI,B.aCO,B.aCG,B.aCH,B.aCz,B.aCK,B.aCD,B.aCM,B.aCF,B.aCB],t.mA)
